{"Title":"An Act relative to mandated reporters of disabled persons abuse","BillNumber":"S126","DocketNumber":"SD123","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T16:42:34.08"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T16:42:34.08"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S126/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Tarr, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 126) of Bruce E. Tarr for legislation relative to mandated reporters of disabled persons abuse.  Children, Families and Persons with Disabilities.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 1 of Chapter 19C of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the words “police officer”, in the definition of “Mandated reporter”, the following words:- “, firefighter, emergency medical technician,”.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J13","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J13"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}